rity":"low","title":"bd-d1f76f8089407180 (lifecycle, seq-slow-burst-20): stranded callers are now answered as cancelled","verification":{"evidence":[{"id":"bd-d1f76f8089407180","kind":"behavior"},{"id":"SW-REQ-261006-ZJEY","kind":"requirement"}],"method":"review.behaviorDiff (differential harness run at base and head)","note":"Recorded difference bd-d1f76f8089407180 is classified intended (SW-REQ-261006-ZJEY).","status":"confirmed"}},{"detail":"Our proof work (400a567a) taught test/bdiff/harness.mjs to extract finishDoneFile/releaseNextDoneFile when a revision defines them, to model releaseProc, and to start `property var x: []` queues empty. The base harness on the head tree crashes (`lifecycle: THROW TypeError: finishDoneFile is not a function`) and prints every caller STRANDED. That is why the earlier behaviour diff was discarded. My checks: old and new harness print byte-identical base output on all 14 lifecycle inputs. The new harness prints no THROW, MISSING or COMPILE-ERROR marker at either revision. The only changed lines are `STRANDED` -> `<cancel>`, with equal line counts. One modelling limit: releaseProc is modelled as finishing before the next event. The real queue drains each write on onExited, so the same callers are answered, but not necessarily before the next event.","refs":[{"id":"test/bdiff/harness.mjs","kind":"file","line":161},{"id":"test/bdiff/harness.mjs","kind":"file","line":243},{"id":"test/bdiff/harness.mjs","kind":"file","line":321},{"id":"test/bdiff/harness.mjs","kind":"test"}],"severity":"info","title":"My run: the 14 differences are behaviour, not artefacts of the harness fix","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"untyped finding","note":"No typed claim: this finding is the author's judgement and is not checked against the package.","status":"unverifiable"}},{"claim":{"params":{"relatesTo":["bin/omarchy-menu-select","bin/omarchy-menu-input","bin/omarchy-menu-handshake:wait_for_menu_done"],"scenario":"omarchy.menu listed in disabledPlugins: omarchy-menu-select summons, omarchy-shell prints 'unknown' and exits 0, the shell stays alive, and the caller polls with no end"},"type":"behavior_hazard"},"detail":"The IPC summon returns \"unknown\" when shell.summon() is false, for example when omarchy.menu is in disabledPlugins (shell.qml summon handler; the plugin-not-enabled branch). omarchy-shell prints the reply and exits 0 (bin/omarchy-shell:123-125, and :79-87 on the socket path). select:98 and input:57 discard stdout, so the new exit-status check never fires. The shell stays alive, so the liveness check never fires either, and the caller waits on as before. images:449 already compares the reply to \"ok\". We saw this live with a real quickshell in a headless session: reply `unknown`, exit 0, picker still waiting at 8s on base and head, and exit 1 at once with a reply check. That run is outside the package.","refs":[{"id":"bin/omarchy-menu-select","kind":"file","line":98},{"id":"bin/omarchy-menu-input","kind":"file","line":57},{"id":"bin/omarchy-menu-images","kind":"file","line":449},{"id":"bin/omarchy-shell","kind":"file","line":123},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-Q6ZS","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-9ABD","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"medium","title":"Question: should a summon the shell refuses with `unknown` fail the caller, as omarchy-menu-images already does?","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"behavior hazard: settled only by a recorded test outcome","note":"A runtime-behavior question the package's static facts cannot settle; it needs a test. Suggested test: \"Refused summon: stub omarchy-shell prints `unknown` and exits 0\".","status":"needs_test"}},{"claim":{"params":{"relatesTo":["bin/omarchy-menu-handshake:menu_shell_pid","bin/omarchy-menu-handshake:wait_for_menu_done"],"scenario":"two accounts each running quickshell -p /usr/share/omarchy/shell; the other account's shell has the lower pid; omarchy-menu-select records it, kill -0 fails with EPERM, and the caller exits 1 about a second in while its picker is still open"},"type":"behavior_hazard"},"detail":"`pgrep -x quickshell` (handshake:26) lists every user's processes, and /proc/<pid>/cmdline is world-readable by default. With the packaged OMARCHY_PATH=/usr/share/omarchy, two accounts' shells both contain \"/usr/share/omarchy/shell\". The first in pgrep order (lowest pid) wins. `kill -0` on another user's pid fails with EPERM, so wait_for_menu_done returns 1 at the first $SECONDS tick (handshake:51) while the caller's own menu is still on screen. My model with an unsignalable pid (pid 1 on macOS) returned 1 after 0.14-0.7s in 3 runs, though the done file was written at 2.5s. `pgrep -u \"$UID\" -x quickshell` would scope the lookup. Two sessions of the same user on different WAYLAND_DISPLAYs are a related case that -u does not cover. Not staged on a real two-account machine.","refs":[{"id":"bin/omarchy-menu-handshake","kind":"file","line":26},{"id":"bin/omarchy-menu-handshake","kind":"file","line":51},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-Q6ZS","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-MH9B","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"medium","title":"Question: can menu_shell_pid pick another account's shell, so a live picker is abandoned after about a second?","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"behavior hazard: settled only by a recorded test outcome","note":"A runtime-behavior question the package's static facts cannot settle; it needs a test. Suggested test: \"Pid lookup ignores another account's shell\".","status":"needs_test"}},{"claim":{"params":{"relatesTo":["bin/omarchy-menu-select","bin/omarchy-menu-handshake:menu_shell_pid"],"scenario":"omarchy-restart-shell runs after menu_shell_pid but before the summon: the new shell shows the picker while the caller exits 1 on the old pid"},"type":"behavior_hazard"},"detail":"select:93 resolves the pid before the summon at :98. If omarchy-restart-shell replaces the shell in that window, the new shell takes the request and shows the picker, but the caller watches the old pid. It exits 1 (\"the shell exited before answering\") about a second later, and the user's later pick is written to a done file nobody reads. The window is short. Reading the pid after the summon, or retrying once, would close it.","refs":[{"id":"bin/omarchy-menu-select","kind":"file","line":93},{"id":"bin/omarchy-menu-select","kind":"file","line":98},{"id":"bin/omarchy-menu-handshake","kind":"file","line":51},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-Q6ZS","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"low","title":"Question: what happens when the shell restarts between the pid lookup and the summon?","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"behavior hazard: settled only by a recorded test outcome","note":"A runtime-behavior question the package's static facts cannot settle; it needs a test. Suggested test: \"Shell replaced between pid lookup and summon\".","status":"needs_test"}},{"claim":{"params":{"relatesTo":["shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml:finishDoneFile","bin/omarchy-menu-handshake:wait_for_menu_done"],"scenario":"a select request is pending (or queued in doneFilesToRelease) when the menu plugin is disabled or rescanned while quickshell keeps running: the caller is never answered"},"type":"behavior_hazard"},"detail":"The PR says so itself (\"Known remaining edge\"): the menu plugin can be destroyed while a request is pending, but Quickshell stays alive, so the liveness check sees a healthy owner. doneFilesToRelease (Menu.qml:75) also lives in the component, so queued releases not yet written are lost with it. Only a test with a live plugin reload can settle how often this happens.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":75},{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":156},{"id":"SW-REQ-261006-ZJEY","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SYS-REQ-260922-X6Z5","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"low","title":"Question: a request pending when the menu plugin is torn down (rescan or disable) is still stranded; is the PR's stated edge acceptable?","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"behavior hazard: settled only by a recorded test outcome","note":"A runtime-behavior question the package's static facts cannot settle; it needs a test. Suggested test: \"Plugin teardown with a pending request\".","status":"needs_test"}},{"detail":"finishRequest still clears the request and then sets resultProc.running = true. Quickshell ignores that while the previous write runs. In my replay, `S P S C` (A answered, B summoned and dismissed within the same write) leaves B STRANDED at base and at this head. The behaviour diff shows no difference for `S A S P` (interleave-01) for the same reason. This is the busy-writer leg of KI-MENU-REQUEST-LIFECYCLE (still open). #9056 at b7bd59c4 answers it with Quickshell.execDetached.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":124},{"id":"proof/known-issues/KI-MENU-REQUEST-LIFECYCLE.yaml","kind":"file","line":2},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-FGZQ","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-C8HX","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"info","title":"Not changed by this PR: a pick made while resultProc is still writing is still lost","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"untyped finding","note":"No typed claim: this finding is the author's judgement and is not checked against the package.","status":"unverifiable"}},{"detail":"c88f3f07 applies the upstream diff. Its +/- lines are identical to the upstream PR's three commits. Later commits are ours. c254528b/b32a4213: the KI-MENU-SELECT-POLL-DEADLOCK reproducer kills a stand-in shell after the summon. b9bf86f6/0ca7725f: that KI is marked fixed and recaptured not reproduced. d24499a3: stand-in shells in the dmenu and images tests, external_call_timeout_bounded witnesses, and Implements annotations (comment lines only). be83388f: trace reviews. 90ea48e0: verification states re-derived. 400a567a: harness. 91f3ce4a/78bebe32/fe73f473: the #9057 report and the lifecycle KI. baccec87/113f329b/f673f43e: SW-REQ-261006-ZJEY, its review record, the node